<section>
    <h2>Density-Aware Typography</h2>

    <p>High-density displays render CSS pixels using more physical pixels. For optimal readability, typography can be
        adjusted based on density.</p>

    <h3>fluid_type_density() Mixin</h3>

    <p>Extends fluid typography with density awareness. High-DPR screens get proportionally smaller text to maintain
        optical consistency:</p>

    <div class="code-block"><pre><code>html {
        <span class="comment">// Base fluid type: 12px → 24px from 360px → 4320px viewport</span>
        @include fluid_type_density(360px, 4320px, 12px, 24px);
        }

        <span class="comment">// With custom density scale (default: 0.9 = 10% reduction per DPR step)</span>
        html {
        @include fluid_type_density(360px, 4320px, 12px, 24px, 0.95);
        }</code></pre></div>

    <p>This generates:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>1× DPR:</strong> 12px → 24px fluid scaling</li>
        <li><strong>2× DPR:</strong> 10.8px → 21.6px (×0.9)</li>
        <li><strong>3× DPR:</strong> 9.72px → 19.44px (×0.81)</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>q_density() Function</h3>

    <p>Runtime density-aware Q units using the JavaScript-injected <code>--dpr-inverse</code>:</p>

    <div class="code-block"><pre><code>.element {
        font-size: q_density(16); <span class="comment">// Scales with runtime DPR</span>
        padding: q_density(8);
        line-height: q_density(24);
        }

        <span class="comment">// Compiles to:</span>
        .element {
        font-size: calc(1rem * var(--dpr-inverse, 1));
        padding: calc(0.5rem * var(--dpr-inverse, 1));
        line-height: calc(1.5rem * var(--dpr-inverse, 1));
        }</code></pre></div>

    <h3>scale_density() Functions</h3>

    <p>Retrieve typographic scale values adjusted for density:</p>

    <div class="code-block"><pre><code><span class="comment">// Compile-time density adjustment</span>
        font-size: scale_density(7); <span class="comment">// q(16) at 1× DPR</span>
        font-size: scale_density(7, 2); <span class="comment">// q(16) × 0.9 at 2× DPR</span>
        font-size: scale_density(7, 3); <span class="comment">// q(16) × 0.81 at 3× DPR</span>

        <span class="comment">// Runtime density adjustment (requires JS injection)</span>
        font-size: scale_density_runtime(7); <span class="comment">// Scales with --dpr-inverse</span></code></pre></div>

</section>
